Subject: Record allocation-site property counts and learned capacities

What this does
  A constructor's learned instance inline capacity and the highest instance
  property count it was seen to reach are written on its `F` line; an object
  literal's final property count is written as `props=` on its allocation
  site's `P` line.

Why we need it
  A pre-sized allocation in the final shape is worth a transition per property
  and a dependent field access per read, and the data to size it is exactly
  what the engine already learns at run time. Nothing put it in the profile.

What it adds
  `JSAotProfPc.alloc_props`, `js_aot_prof_alloc`, `inst_cap=`/`inst_seen=` on
  the `F` line and `props=` on the `P` line; `profmerge.py` merges them.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

